{% extends "layouts/app-layout.njk" %}

{% set pageTitle = "Updating to version 11" %}
{% set pageDescription = "How to update your service or prototype to version 11 of the NHS.UK frontend library and design system." %}
{% set pageSection = "Design system" %}
{% set subSection = "Design system" %}
{% set theme = "Update guides" %}
{% set dateUpdated = "November 2026" %}

{% block beforeContent %}
  {% include "design-system/_breadcrumb.njk" %}
{% endblock %}

{% block bodyContent %}
  <p>Version 11 introduces a number of breaking changes.</p>

  <p>Follow this guide carefully when applying updates to make sure your service does not break.</p>

  <p><a href="/design-system/production">Learn more about the NHS.UK frontend library</a>.</p>

  {{ insetText({
    classes: "nhsuk-u-margin-top-4",
    text: "If you are using a build of the design system in another language or framework, for example React or a Wordpress theme, you may need the maintainer of that tool to follow these updates to support version 11 before you can upgrade."
  }) }}

  {{ contentsList({
    items: [
      {
        href: "#stylesheets",
        text: "Stylesheets"
      },
      {
        href: "#javascript",
        text: "JavaScript"
      },
      {
        href: "#page-template",
        text: "Page template"
      },
      {
        href: "#components",
        text: "Components"
      },
      {
        href: "#sass-functions",
        text: "Sass functions, mixins and variables"
      }
    ]
  }) }}

  <h2 id="stylesheets">Stylesheets</h2>

  <h3 id="rename-sass-grid-column-parameter">Rename Sass grid column parameter</h3>

  <p>We've renamed the <code>$at</code> parameter of the <code>nhsuk-grid-column</code> Sass mixin to <code>$from</code>, matching grid column classes ending <code>-from-mobile</code> and <code>-from-desktop</code>.</p>

  <p>If you're using the <code>nhsuk-grid-column</code> Sass mixin to create custom grid classes, you should rename <code>$at</code> to <code>$from</code>:</p>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      .app-grid-column-one-quarter-from-desktop {
      -   @include nhsuk-grid-column(one-quarter, $at: desktop);
      +   @include nhsuk-grid-column(one-quarter, $from: desktop);
      }
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <p>You can still use the <code>$at</code> parameter but we'll remove it in a future breaking release.</p>

  <h3 id="mobile-width-override-classes">Mobile width override classes</h3>

  <p>Grid column classes ending <code>-from-mobile</code> are applied at mobile width (320px) and above.</p>

  <p>If you're using the following mobile width utility classes, you must:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>replace <code>nhsuk-u-one-half</code> with <code>nhsuk-grid-column-one-half-from-mobile</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>nhsuk-u-one-third</code> with <code>nhsuk-grid-column-one-third-from-mobile</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>nhsuk-u-two-thirds</code> with <code>nhsuk-grid-column-two-thirds-from-mobile</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>nhsuk-u-one-quarter</code> with <code>nhsuk-grid-column-one-quarter-from-mobile</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>nhsuk-u-three-quarters</code> with <code>nhsuk-grid-column-three-quarters-from-mobile</code></li>
  </ul>

  <h3 id="tablet-width-override-classes">Tablet width override classes</h3>

  <p>Grid column classes not ending <code>-from-mobile</code> or <code>-from-desktop</code> are applied at tablet width (641px) and above.</p>

  <p>If you're using the following tablet width utility classes, you must:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>replace <code>nhsuk-u-one-half-tablet</code> with <code>nhsuk-grid-column-one-half</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>nhsuk-u-one-third-tablet</code> with <code>nhsuk-grid-column-one-third</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>nhsuk-u-two-thirds-tablet</code> with <code>nhsuk-grid-column-two-thirds</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>nhsuk-u-one-quarter-tablet</code> with <code>nhsuk-grid-column-one-quarter</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>nhsuk-u-three-quarters-tablet</code> with <code>nhsuk-grid-column-three-quarters</code></li>
  </ul>

  <h3 id="nowrap">Make no wrap apply to mobile and above</h3>

  <p>We've updated the <code>nhsuk-u-nowrap</code> utility class to be applied at mobile width (320px and up).</p>

  <p>Previously the utility class did not apply to tablet sized screens (641px and up).</p>

  <p>Please carefully review your pages. If necessary, different wrapping behaviour for the tablet and desktop breakpoints can be applied using new classes ending <code>-from-tablet</code> and <code>-from-desktop</code>.</p>

  <p>To restore the previous behaviour, add the new <code>nhsuk-u-wrap-from-tablet</code> utility class to override the default <code>nhsuk-u-nowrap</code> behaviour for tablet sized screens:</p>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      - <p class="nhsuk-u-nowrap">
      + <p class="nhsuk-u-nowrap nhsuk-u-wrap-from-tablet">
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <h3 id="global-box-sizing-reset-removed">Global box sizing reset removed</h3>

  <p>We have removed the global <code>box-sizing</code> reset and added <code>box-sizing: border-box</code> only where necessary.</p>

  <p>Please review any custom styles, especially those with defined widths, to make sure they have a correctly calculated box size.</p>

  <h3 id="sass-deprecated-load-paths-removed">Sass deprecated load paths removed</h3>

  <p>We've removed the Sass <code>nhsuk/nhsuk</code> and <code>/all</code> import paths that were deprecated in version 9.5.0.</p>

  <p>If you're importing the core NHS.UK frontend Sass only, or individual Sass layers such as settings or tools, you must remove <code>/all</code> from each path:</p>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      - @import "nhsuk-frontend/packages/core/all";
      + @import "nhsuk-frontend/packages/core";

      - @import "nhsuk-frontend/packages/core/settings/all";
      - @import "nhsuk-frontend/packages/core/tools/all";
      + @import "nhsuk-frontend/packages/core/settings";
      + @import "nhsuk-frontend/packages/core/tools";
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <p>If you're importing the <code>nhsuk/nhsuk</code> Sass entry point, you must import <code>nhsuk</code> instead:</p>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      - @import "nhsuk-frontend/dist/nhsuk/nhsuk";
      + @import "nhsuk-frontend/dist/nhsuk";
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <p>If you're importing individual component Sass partials, you must remove the duplicate component name from each path:</p>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      - @import "nhsuk-frontend/dist/nhsuk/components/action-link/action-link";
      - @import "nhsuk-frontend/dist/nhsuk/components/back-link/back-link";
      - @import "nhsuk-frontend/dist/nhsuk/components/button/button";
      + @import "nhsuk-frontend/dist/nhsuk/components/action-link";
      + @import "nhsuk-frontend/dist/nhsuk/components/back-link";
      + @import "nhsuk-frontend/dist/nhsuk/components/button";
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <h3 id="sass-variable-for-secondary-border-colour-updated">Sass variable for secondary border colour updated</h3>

  <p>We've changed the Sass variable <code>$nhsuk-secondary-border-colour</code> from <code>rgba(nhsuk-colour("white"), 0.2)</code> to <code>nhsuk-colour("grey-3")</code>.</p>

  <p>To restore the previous colour, either replace <code>$nhsuk-secondary-border-colour</code> with <code>$nhsuk-reverse-border-colour</code> for blue backgrounds, or replace it with <code>rgba(nhsuk-colour("white"), 0.2)</code> to preserve transparency.</p>

  <h3 id="link-styles">Links are easier to read and have a clearer hover state</h3>

  <p>Links now have underlines that are consistently thinner and a bit further away from the link text.</p>

  <p>Links also have a clearer hover state using dark blue (<code>#003087</code>) instead of dark pink (<code>#7c2855</code>), where the underline gets thicker to make the link stand out to users.</p>

  <p>Please carefully review your pages. If you have created your own link styles, you should review them to ensure their use is consistent across your service.</p>

  <h2 id="javascript">JavaScript</h2>

  <h3 id="deprecated-component-init-functions-removed">Deprecated component init functions removed</h3>

  <p>We've replaced component init functions with the <code>createAll</code> function added in version 10.0.0.</p>

  <p>If you're using functions such as <code>initButtons</code> and <code>initCheckboxes</code>, you must replace them with the <code>createAll</code> function:</p>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      - import { initButtons, initCheckboxes } from 'nhsuk-frontend'
      + import { createAll, Button, Checkboxes } from 'nhsuk-frontend'

      - initButtons()
      - initCheckboxes()
      + createAll(Button)
      + createAll(Checkboxes)
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <p>Where a component config object or scope is required, these can also be passed to the <code>createAll</code> function:</p>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      - import { initButtons, initCheckboxes } from 'nhsuk-frontend'
      + import { createAll, Button, Checkboxes } from 'nhsuk-frontend'

        const $element = document.querySelector('.app-modal')

      - initButtons({
      + createAll(Button, {
          preventDoubleClick: true,
          scope: $element,
        })

      - initCheckboxes({ scope: $element })
      + createAll(Checkboxes, $element)
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <h3 id="deprecated-javascript-options-removed">Deprecated JavaScript options removed</h3>

  <p>We've removed the deprecated <code>focusOnPageLoad</code> option from the error summary component JavaScript. You must use the <code>disableAutoFocus</code> JavaScript API option instead:</p>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("js") %}
      import { createAll, ErrorSummary } from 'nhsuk-frontend'

      createAll(ErrorSummary, {
        disableAutoFocus: true
      })
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <p>We've also removed the deprecated <code>jsHiddenClass</code> property from the tabs component JavaScript. You must use the <code>panelClass</code> JavaScript API option instead:</p>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("js") %}
      import { createAll, Tabs } from 'nhsuk-frontend'

      createAll(Tabs, {
        panelClass: 'nhsuk-tabs__panel'
      })
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <p>The modifier <code>--hidden</code> is appended automatically to <code>panelClass</code> when used to hide a tab panel.</p>

  <h2 id="page-template">Page template</h2>

  <h3 id="apply-grid-column-widths-from-tablet">Apply grid column widths from tablet (not desktop) width</h3>

  <p>We've updated our grid column styles to be applied at tablet width (641px and up).</p>

  <p>Previously they were applied from desktop width (769px and up), making it difficult to cater for smaller screen sizes.</p>

  <p>Please carefully review your pages. If necessary, different grid behaviour for the mobile and desktop breakpoints can be applied using new classes ending <code>-from-mobile</code> and <code>-from-desktop</code>.</p>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      - <div class="nhsuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
      + <div class="nhsuk-grid-column-three-quarters nhsuk-grid-column-two-thirds-from-desktop">
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <h2 id="components">Components</h2>

  <p>Many deprecated Nunjucks options and HTML classes have been removed. If you use Nunjucks macros, update the options below. If you write the HTML yourself, use the examples on the relevant component page.</p>

  <h3 id="action-links-back-links-and-buttons">Action links, back links and buttons</h3>

  <p>The deprecated <code>element</code> option has been removed from action links, back links and buttons. Components now use an anchor when <code>href</code> is set and a button otherwise. Button components no longer support the <code>&lt;input&gt;</code> element. For a button, use <code>type</code> instead:</p>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      actionLink({
        text: "Action link",
      - element: "button"
      + type: "submit"
      })
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <h3 id="breadcrumbs">Breadcrumbs</h3>

  <p>For the <code>breadcrumb</code> macro, replace <code>labelText</code> with <code>ariaLabel</code>. Move the current page's top-level <code>text</code> and <code>href</code> into the <code>items</code> array.</p>

  <h3 id="cards">Cards</h3>

  <p>For the <code>card</code> macro:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>replace <code>imgURL</code> with <code>image.src</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>imgALT</code> with <code>image.alt</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>feature: true</code> with <code>variant: "feature"</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>primary: true</code> with <code>variant: "primary"</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>secondary: true</code> with <code>variant: "secondary"</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>warning: true</code> with <code>variant: "warning"</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>type: "non-urgent"</code> with <code>variant: "non-urgent"</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>type: "urgent"</code> with <code>variant: "urgent"</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>type: "emergency"</code> with <code>variant: "emergency"</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>headingHtml</code> with <code>heading.html</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>headingClasses</code> with <code>heading.classes</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>headingId</code> with <code>heading.id</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>headingSize</code> with <code>heading.size</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>headingLevel</code> with <code>heading.level</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>headingVisuallyHiddenText</code> with <code>heading.visuallyHiddenText</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>descriptionHtml</code> with <code>description.html</code></li>
  </ul>

  <p>If you are not using the Nunjucks macro, update the card classes as follows:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>add the missing <code>nhsuk-card--primary</code> modifier class to primary cards</li>
    <li>remove the <code>nhsuk-card__heading--feature</code> modifier class from feature card headings</li>
    <li>remove the <code>nhsuk-card__content--feature</code> modifier class from feature card content</li>
    <li>remove the <code>nhsuk-card__content--primary</code> modifier class from primary card content</li>
    <li>remove the <code>nhsuk-card__content--secondary</code> modifier class from secondary card content</li>
    <li>rename <code>nhsuk-card--care__heading-container</code> to <code>nhsuk-card__heading-container</code></li>
    <li>rename <code>nhsuk-card--care__heading</code> to <code>nhsuk-card__heading</code></li>
  </ul>

  <h3 id="character-count">Character count</h3>

  <p>Replace <code>maxwords</code> with <code>maxlength</code> and <code>countType: "words"</code>. The default <code>countType</code> is now <code>"characters"</code>, so you can remove <code>countType: "characters"</code>. Remove the deprecated <code>nhsuk-character-count__status--disabled</code> and <code>nhsuk-character-count__message--disabled</code> classes.</p>

  <p>If you're using the JavaScript API, make the same change:</p>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
        new CharacterCount($root, {
      -   maxwords: 150
      +   maxlength: 150,
      +   countType: 'words'
        })
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <p>If you are not using the Nunjucks macro, add the <code>hidden</code> attribute to an:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>empty visible count message with a <code>threshold</code> set but not yet reached</li>
    <li>empty textarea description with neither <code>maxlength</code> nor <code>maxwords</code> set</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 id="checkboxes-and-radios">Checkboxes and radios</h3>

  <p>For exclusive checkboxes, replace <code>exclusive</code> with <code>behaviour: "exclusive"</code>, and rename <code>exclusiveGroup</code> to <code>behaviourGroup</code>.</p>
  <p>In hand-written HTML, use <code>data-behaviour</code> and <code>data-behaviour-group</code>.</p>

  <p>For conditionally revealed checkboxes and radios, replace <code>aria-controls</code> with <code>data-aria-controls</code>.</p>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      <input type="checkbox" value="none"
      - data-checkbox-exclusive
      - data-checkbox-exclusive-group="preferences"
      + data-behaviour="exclusive"
      + data-behaviour-group="preferences">

      <input type="radio" value="email"
      - aria-controls="conditional-email"
      + data-aria-controls="conditional-email">
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <h3 id="contents-list">Contents list</h3>

  <p>For the <code>contentsList</code> macro, rename <code>landmarkLabel</code> to <code>ariaLabel</code>.</p>

  <h3 id="details">Details</h3>

  <p>For the <code>details</code> macro, replace <code>summaryText</code> and <code>summaryHtml</code> with <code>summary.text</code> and <code>summary.html</code>.</p>

  <h3 id="do-and-dont-lists">Do and don't lists</h3>

  <p>For the <code>list</code> macro:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>replace <code>title</code> with <code>heading.text</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>headingLevel</code> with <code>heading.level</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>type: "tick"</code> and <code>type: "cross"</code> with <code>icon: "tick"</code> and <code>icon: "cross"</code></li>
    <li>use <code>text</code> or <code>html</code> instead of <code>item</code> for each item</li>
  </ul>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      {% raw %}
      {{ list({
      -   title: "Do",
      -   headingLevel: 3,
      -   type: "tick",
      +   heading: {
      +     text: "Do",
      +     level: 3
      +   },
      +   icon: "tick",
          items: [
            {
      -       item: "cover blisters with a soft plaster or padded dressing"
      +       text: "cover blisters with a soft plaster or padded dressing"
            }
          ]
      }) }}
      {% endraw %}
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <p>Hand-written HTML lists should use card classes and rename <code>nhsuk-icon__tick</code> to <code>nhsuk-icon--tick</code> and <code>nhsuk-icon__cross</code> to <code>nhsuk-icon--cross</code>:</p>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      + <div class="nhsuk-card nhsuk-card--feature">
      -   <div class="nhsuk-do-dont-list">
      -     <h3 class="nhsuk-do-dont-list__label">Do</h3>
      +   <div class="nhsuk-card__content">
      +     <h3 class="nhsuk-card__heading">Do</h3>
          <ul class="nhsuk-list nhsuk-list--tick" role="list">
            <li>
      -       <svg class="nhsuk-icon nhsuk-icon__tick" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
      +       <svg class="nhsuk-icon nhsuk-icon--tick" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                <!-- Tick icon -->
              </svg>
              cover blisters with a soft plaster or padded dressing
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      + </div>
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <h3 id="error-summary">Error summary</h3>

  <p>Replace the title and description options with nested <code>heading</code> and <code>description</code> options. If you write the HTML yourself, follow the updated examples: remove <code>aria-labelledby</code>, <code>role="alert"</code> and <code>tabindex</code> from the outer element, put <code>role="alert"</code> on a wrapper around its contents, and rename <code>nhsuk-error-summary__title</code> to <code>nhsuk-error-summary__heading</code>.</p>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      - <div class="nhsuk-error-summary" aria-labelledby="error-summary-title" role="alert" tabindex="-1">
      + <div class="nhsuk-error-summary">
      +   <div role="alert">
      -     <h2 class="nhsuk-error-summary__title" id="error-summary-title">
      +     <h2 class="nhsuk-error-summary__heading">
            There is a problem
          </h2>
        </div>
      </div>
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <h3 id="error-message">Error message</h3>

  <p>The HTML for error messages now uses a <code>&lt;p&gt;</code> element instead of a <code>&lt;span&gt;</code> element.</p>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      - <span class="nhsuk-error-message">
      + <p class="nhsuk-error-message">
          <span class="nhsuk-u-visually-hidden">Error:</span> Example error message
      - </span>
      + </p>
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <h3 id="header-and-footer">Header and footer</h3>

  <p>Update deprecated header options as follows:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>replace <code>search.placeholder</code> with <code>search.input.placeholder</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>search.visuallyHiddenLabel</code> with <code>search.label.visuallyHiddenText</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>search.visuallyHiddenButton</code> with <code>search.button.ariaLabel</code></li>
  </ul>

  <p>The header search now uses the search input component. If you write the HTML yourself, use the <a href="/design-system/components/header">header examples</a>.</p>

  <p>If not done already, apply the changes from version 10.3.0:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>add the <code>novalidate</code> boolean attribute to the search form element and account item forms</li>
    <li>add the <code>&lt;div class="nhsuk-form-group"&gt;</code> wrapper around the search label, input and button</li>
    <li>add the <code>&lt;div class="nhsuk-input-wrapper"&gt;</code> wrapper around the search input and button</li>
    <li>add the <code>nhsuk-button</code> and <code>nhsuk-button--small</code> classes to the search button</li>
    <li>remove the <code>nhsuk-header__search-submit</code> class from the search button</li>
    <li>remove the <code>nhsuk-header__search-input</code> class from the search input</li>
  </ul>

  <p>If not done already, apply the changes from version 10.5.0:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>add the <code>aria-label="Search"</code> attribute to the search button</li>
    <li>remove the <code>aria-label="Search"</code> and <code>role="img"</code> attributes, and the <code>&lt;title&gt;</code> child element, from the search icon SVG</li>
    <li>add the <code>aria-hidden="true"</code> attribute to the search icon SVG</li>
    <li>update the search icon SVG path</li>
  </ul>

  <p>Finally, apply the changes to use the search input component:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>add the <code>nhsuk-search-input</code> class to the <code>nhsuk-form-group</code> element</li>
    <li>add the <code>nhsuk-search-input__wrapper</code> class to the <code>nhsuk-input-wrapper</code> element</li>
    <li>add the <code>nhsuk-search-input__input</code> class to the search input</li>
    <li>add the <code>nhsuk-search-input__button</code> class to the search button</li>
    <li>add the <code>nhsuk-button--brand-reverse</code> class to the search button for the blue header, or <code>nhsuk-button--brand</code> for the white header</li>
  </ul>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      - <div class="nhsuk-form-group">
      + <div class="nhsuk-form-group nhsuk-search-input">
          <label class="nhsuk-label nhsuk-u-visually-hidden" for="search-field">
            Search the NHS website
          </label>
      -   <div class="nhsuk-input-wrapper">
      -     <input class="nhsuk-input" id="search-field" name="q" type="search" autocomplete="off" placeholder="Search">
      -     <button class="nhsuk-button nhsuk-button--icon nhsuk-button--small" data-module="nhsuk-button" type="submit" aria-label="Search">
      +   <div class="nhsuk-input-wrapper nhsuk-search-input__wrapper">
      +     <input class="nhsuk-input nhsuk-search-input__input" id="search-field" name="q" type="search" autocomplete="off" placeholder="Search">
      +     <button class="nhsuk-button nhsuk-button--brand-reverse nhsuk-button--icon nhsuk-button--small nhsuk-search-input__button" data-module="nhsuk-button" type="submit" aria-label="Search">
              <!-- Search icon -->
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <p>For the <code>footer</code> macro, replace <code>navigation.title</code> with <code>navigation.heading.text</code>, and rename <code>meta.visuallyHiddenTitle</code> to <code>meta.visuallyHiddenText</code>.</p>

  <h3 id="hero">Hero</h3>

  <p>For the <code>hero</code> macro, move image options into <code>image.src</code> and heading options into <code>heading</code>. In hand-written HTML, use <code>nhsuk-hero__content</code> and place <code>nhsuk-hero__overlay</code> below the width container:</p>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      <section class="nhsuk-hero nhsuk-hero--image">
      - <div class="nhsuk-hero__overlay">
          <div class="nhsuk-width-container">
            <div class="nhsuk-grid-row">
              <div class="nhsuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
      -         <div class="nhsuk-hero-content">
      +         <div class="nhsuk-hero__content">
                  <!-- Hero content -->
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
      - </div>
      + <div class="nhsuk-hero__overlay"></div>
      </section>
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <p>For heroes without images, move the <code>nhsuk-hero--border</code> class to the top-level and rename <code>nhsuk-hero__wrapper</code> to <code>nhsuk-hero__content</code>:</p>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      - <section class="nhsuk-hero">
      -   <div class="nhsuk-width-container nhsuk-hero--border">
      + <section class="nhsuk-hero nhsuk-hero--border">
      +   <div class="nhsuk-width-container">
            <div class="nhsuk-grid-row">
              <div class="nhsuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
      -         <div class="nhsuk-hero__wrapper">
      +         <div class="nhsuk-hero__content">
                  <!-- Hero content -->
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <h3 id="input">Input</h3>

  <p>We've removed HTML classes for inputs that were deprecated in versions 10.2.0 and 10.3.0. If you are not using the Nunjucks macros, you must change the input classes as follows:</p>

  <ul>
    <li><code>nhsuk-input__wrapper</code> to <code>nhsuk-input-wrapper</code></li>
    <li><code>nhsuk-input__prefix</code> to <code>nhsuk-input-wrapper__prefix</code></li>
    <li><code>nhsuk-input__suffix</code> to <code>nhsuk-input-wrapper__suffix</code></li>
  </ul>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      - <div class="nhsuk-input__wrapper">
      -   <span class="nhsuk-input__prefix">£</span>
      + <div class="nhsuk-input-wrapper">
      +   <span class="nhsuk-input-wrapper__prefix">£</span>
          <input class="nhsuk-input" type="text">
        </div>
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <h3 id="label-and-legend">Label and legend</h3>

  <p>We've removed the <code>isPageHeading</code> Nunjucks option for labels and legends. If you're using any form component Nunjucks macro with this option, rename the <code>text</code> option to <code>heading</code> and remove <code>isPageHeading: true</code>.</p>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      characterCount({
        label: {
      -   text: "Can you provide more detail?",
      +   heading: "Can you provide more detail?",
      -   isPageHeading: true,
          size: "l"
        },
        name: "more-detail",
        maxlength: 350,
        countType: "characters"
      })
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <h3 id="notification-banners">Notification banners</h3>

  <p>In the <code>notificationBanner</code> macro:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>replace <code>type: "success"</code> with <code>variant: "success"</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>titleText</code>, <code>titleHtml</code> and <code>titleId</code> with <code>title.text</code>, <code>title.html</code> and <code>title.id</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>titleHeadingLevel</code> with <code>title.level</code></li>
  </ul>

  <h3 id="panels">Panels</h3>

  <p>In the <code>panel</code> macro, move title options into a nested <code>heading</code> object.</p>

  <p>For hand-written HTML, rename the panel heading class <code>nhsuk-panel__title</code> to <code>nhsuk-panel__heading</code>, and the <code>nhsuk-panel__title--xl</code>, <code>nhsuk-panel__title--l</code> and <code>nhsuk-panel__title--m</code> modifier classes to <code>nhsuk-panel__heading--xl</code>, <code>nhsuk-panel__heading--l</code> and <code>nhsuk-panel__heading--m</code>:</p>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      - <h1 class="nhsuk-panel__title nhsuk-panel__title--l">
      + <h1 class="nhsuk-panel__heading nhsuk-panel__heading--l">
          Panel heading
        </h1>
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <h3 id="pagination">Pagination</h3>

  <p>In the <code>pagination</code> macro:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>replace <code>previousUrl</code> with <code>previous.href</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>previousPage</code> with <code>previous.label</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>nextUrl</code> with <code>next.href</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>nextPage</code> with <code>next.label</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>previous.labelText</code> with <code>previous.label</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>next.labelText</code> with <code>next.label</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>landmarkLabel</code> with <code>ariaLabel</code></li>
    <li>replace <code>visuallyHiddenText</code> for <code>items</code> with <code>item.ariaLabel</code></li>
  </ul>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      {% raw %}
      {{ pagination({
      -   landmarkLabel: "Guide pages",
      -   previousPage: "Before you apply",
      -   previousUrl: "/guide/before-you-apply",
      -   nextPage: "After you apply",
      -   nextUrl: "/guide/after-you-apply"
      +   ariaLabel: "Guide pages",
      +   previous: {
      +     label: "Before you apply",
      +     href: "/guide/before-you-apply"
      +   },
      +   next: {
      +     label: "After you apply",
      +     href: "/guide/after-you-apply"
      +   }
      }) }}
      {% endraw %}
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <h3 id="password-input">Password input</h3>

  <p>In the <code>passwordInput</code> macro:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>Rename <code>showPasswordAriaLabelText</code> to <code>showPasswordAriaLabel</code>.</li>
    <li>Rename <code>hidePasswordAriaLabelText</code> to <code>hidePasswordAriaLabel</code>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 id="tabs">Tabs</h3>

  <p>In the <code>tabs</code> macro, rename the <code>title</code> option to <code>visuallyHiddenText</code>.</p>

  <p>For hand-written HTML, rename the heading class from <code>nhsuk-tabs__title</code> to <code>nhsuk-tabs__heading</code>:</p>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      - <h2 class="nhsuk-tabs__title">Contents</h2>
      + <h2 class="nhsuk-tabs__heading">Contents</h2>
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <h3 id="tables">Tables</h3>

  <p>In the <code>table</code> macro:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>Replace <code>panel: true</code> with <code>card.variant: "feature"</code>.</li>
    <li>Move <code>heading</code> to <code>card.heading.text</code>.</li>
    <li>Move <code>headingLevel</code> to <code>card.heading.level</code>.</li>
    <li>Move <code>panelClasses</code> to <code>card.classes</code>.</li>
    <li>Rename <code>tableClasses</code> to <code>classes</code>.</li>
    <li>If you set <code>captionSize</code> or <code>captionClasses</code>, use a <code>caption</code> object with <code>text</code>, <code>size</code> and <code>classes</code> as needed.</li>
    <li>For responsive tables, remove <code>header</code> from each cell in <code>rows</code>. The macro uses the column headings from <code>head</code>.</li>
  </ul>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      {% raw %}
      {{ table({
      -   panel: true,
      -   heading: "Clinic opening times",
      -   headingLevel: 3,
      -   panelClasses: "app-clinic-card",
      -   tableClasses: "app-clinic-table",
      -   caption: "Weekday appointments",
      -   captionSize: "m",
      -   captionClasses: "app-clinic-caption",
      +   card: {
      +     variant: "feature",
      +     heading: {
      +       text: "Clinic opening times",
      +       level: 3
      +     },
      +     classes: "app-clinic-card"
      +   },
      +   classes: "app-clinic-table",
      +   caption: {
      +     text: "Weekday appointments",
      +     size: "m",
      +     classes: "app-clinic-caption"
      +   },
          responsive: true,
          head: [
            { text: "Day" },
            { text: "Opens at" }
          ],
          rows: [
            [
      -       { header: "Day", text: "Monday" },
      -       { header: "Opens at", text: "9am" }
      +       { text: "Monday" },
      +       { text: "9am" }
            ]
          ]
      }) }}
      {% endraw %}
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <p>For HTML tables in panels:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Wrap the table and its heading in a feature card.</li>
    <li>Replace <code>nhsuk-table__panel-with-heading-tab</code> with <code>nhsuk-card__content</code>.</li>
    <li>Replace <code>nhsuk-table__heading-tab</code> with <code>nhsuk-card__heading</code>.</li>
  </ul>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      + <div class="nhsuk-card nhsuk-card--feature">
      -   <div class="nhsuk-table__panel-with-heading-tab">
      +   <div class="nhsuk-card__content">
      -     <h3 class="nhsuk-table__heading-tab">Clinic opening times</h3>
      +     <h3 class="nhsuk-card__heading">Clinic opening times</h3>
            <table class="nhsuk-table">
              <!-- Table headings and rows -->
            </table>
          </div>
      + </div>
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <p>For HTML tables that are responsive:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Replace <code>nhsuk-table-responsive</code> with <code>nhsuk-table nhsuk-table--responsive</code>.</li>
    <li>If you use <code>nhsuk-table-responsive--reverse</code>, replace it with <code>nhsuk-table--reverse</code>.</li>
    <li>Rename <code>nhsuk-table-responsive__heading</code> to <code>nhsuk-table__heading</code>.</li>
  </ul>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      - <table class="nhsuk-table-responsive nhsuk-table-responsive--reverse" role="table">
      + <table class="nhsuk-table nhsuk-table--responsive nhsuk-table--reverse" role="table">
          <thead class="nhsuk-table__head" role="rowgroup">
            <tr class="nhsuk-table__row" role="row">
              <th class="nhsuk-table__header" scope="col" role="columnheader">Opens at</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="nhsuk-table__body" role="rowgroup">
            <tr class="nhsuk-table__row" role="row">
              <td class="nhsuk-table__cell" role="cell">
      -         <span class="nhsuk-table-responsive__heading" aria-hidden="true">Opens at</span>
      +         <span class="nhsuk-table__heading" aria-hidden="true">Opens at</span>
                <span>9am</span>
              </td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <p>For HTML scrolling tables:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Replace <code>nhsuk-table-container</code> with the <code>nhsuk-scroll</code> and add <code>nhsuk-scroll__content</code> wrappers.</li>
    <li>Give the caption a unique <code>id</code> and reference it from <code>aria-labelledby</code> on the inner wrapper.</li>
  </ul>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      - <div class="nhsuk-table-container">
      + <div class="nhsuk-scroll" data-module="nhsuk-scroll">
      +   <div class="nhsuk-scroll__content" role="region" aria-labelledby="clinic-times-caption">
            <table class="nhsuk-table">
      -       <caption class="nhsuk-table__caption">Clinic opening times</caption>
      +       <caption class="nhsuk-table__caption" id="clinic-times-caption">Clinic opening times</caption>
              <!-- Table headings and rows -->
            </table>
      +   </div>
        </div>
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <h3 id="task-list">Task list</h3>

  <p>In the <code>taskList</code> macro, rename each item's <code>title</code> option to <code>heading</code>. To preserve the appearance of completed and cannot-start-yet statuses, replace the removed status classes with a <code>status.tag</code> that has no colour or border:</p>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      {% raw %}
      {{ taskList({
        idPrefix: "application",
        items: [
          {
      -     title: { text: "Check your details" },
      +     heading: { text: "Check your details" },
            href: "/check-details",
            status: {
      -       text: "Completed",
      -       classes: "nhsuk-task-list__status--completed"
      +       tag: {
      +         text: "Completed",
      +         colour: false,
      +         border: false,
      +         classes: "nhsuk-u-font-weight-normal"
      +       }
            }
          }
        ]
      }) }}
      {% endraw %}
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <p>For "Cannot start yet" statuses, replace <code>nhsuk-task-list__status--cannot-start-yet</code> the same way, but also add the <code>nhsuk-u-secondary-text-colour</code> class to the tag, for example <code>classes: "nhsuk-u-font-weight-normal nhsuk-u-secondary-text-colour"</code>.</p>

  <p>For hand-written HTML, remove the old modifier class from the status container and wrap the status text in a tag with no colour or border. This example shows the change for a completed task:</p>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      - <div class="nhsuk-task-list__status nhsuk-task-list__status--completed">
      -   Completed
      + <div class="nhsuk-task-list__status">
      +   <strong class="nhsuk-tag nhsuk-tag--no-colour nhsuk-tag--no-border nhsuk-u-font-weight-normal">Completed</strong>
        </div>
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <p>And for a task that cannot start yet:</p>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      - <div class="nhsuk-task-list__status nhsuk-task-list__status--cannot-start-yet">
      -   Cannot start yet
      + <div class="nhsuk-task-list__status">
      +   <strong class="nhsuk-tag nhsuk-tag--no-colour nhsuk-tag--no-border nhsuk-u-font-weight-normal nhsuk-u-secondary-text-colour">Cannot start yet</strong>
        </div>
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <h3 id="warning-callout">Warning callout</h3>

  <p>In the <code>warningCallout</code> macro, move heading options into <code>heading</code>.</p>

  <p>For hand-written HTML, wrap the callout in a warning card:</p>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      + <div class="nhsuk-card nhsuk-card--warning">
      -   <div class="nhsuk-warning-callout">
      -     <h3 class="nhsuk-warning-callout__label">
      +   <div class="nhsuk-card__content">
      +     <h3 class="nhsuk-card__heading">
            Important<span class="nhsuk-u-visually-hidden">:</span>
          </h3>
        </div>
      + </div>
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <h2 id="sass-functions">Sass functions, mixins and variables</h2>

  <h3 id="colour-variables">Colour variables</h3>

  <p>Use the <code>nhsuk-colour</code> function instead of Sass variables using the old “color” spelling:</p>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      .nhsuk-example {
      -   color: $color_nhsuk-blue;
      +   color: nhsuk-colour("blue");
      }
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <p>Update these Sass variables and CSS classes, for example:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>Replace <code>$nhsuk-link-color</code> with <code>$nhsuk-link-colour</code>.</li>
    <li>Replace <code>$nhsuk-link-hover-color</code> with <code>$nhsuk-link-hover-colour</code>.</li>
    <li>Replace <code>$nhsuk-link-active-color</code> with <code>$nhsuk-link-active-colour</code>.</li>
    <li>Replace <code>$nhsuk-link-visited-color</code> with <code>$nhsuk-link-visited-colour</code>.</li>
    <li>Replace <code>$nhsuk-form-border-color</code> with <code>$nhsuk-input-border-colour</code>.</li>
    <li>Replace <code>$nhsuk-form-element-background-color</code> with <code>$nhsuk-input-background-colour</code>.</li>
    <li>Replace <code>nhsuk-u-secondary-text-color</code> with <code>nhsuk-u-secondary-text-colour</code>.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>See <a href="https://github.com/nhsuk/nhsuk-frontend/pull/1526">NHS.UK frontend pull request #1526</a> for the full list of renamed variables.</p>

  <p>For example, update custom input styles to use the renamed border and background variables:</p>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      .app-input {
      -   border-color: $nhsuk-form-border-color;
      -   background-color: $nhsuk-form-element-background-color;
      +   border-color: $nhsuk-input-border-colour;
      +   background-color: $nhsuk-input-background-colour;
      }
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <h3 id="removed-sass-variables-and-mixins">Removed Sass variables and mixins</h3>

  <h4 id="removed-font-variables">Font variables</h4>

  <p>Update deprecated font variables as follows:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>Combine <code>$nhsuk-font</code> and <code>$nhsuk-font-fallback</code> into one font stack in <code>$nhsuk-font-family</code>.</li>
    <li>Replace <code>$nhsuk-font-normal</code> with <code>$nhsuk-font-weight-normal</code>.</li>
    <li>Replace <code>$nhsuk-font-bold</code> with <code>$nhsuk-font-weight-bold</code>.</li>
    <li>Replace <code>$nhsuk-include-font-face</code> with <code>$nhsuk-include-default-font-face</code>.</li>
    <li>Replace <code>$nhsuk-base-font-size</code> with <code>$nhsuk-root-font-size</code>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h4 id="removed-border-variables">Border variables</h4>

  <p>If your custom styles use the removed border variables:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>Replace <code>$nhsuk-border-width-mobile</code> with <code>$nhsuk-border-width</code>.</li>
    <li>Replace <code>$nhsuk-border-width-form-element-error</code> with <code>$nhsuk-border-width-form-element</code>.</li>
    <li>Replace <code>$nhsuk-border-hover-colour</code> with <code>nhsuk-colour("grey-3")</code> or <code>$nhsuk-secondary-border-colour</code>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h4 id="renamed-sass-mixins">Renamed mixins</h4>

  <ul>
    <li>Replace <code>clearfix</code> with <code>nhsuk-clearfix</code>.</li>
    <li>Replace <code>flex</code> with <code>nhsuk-flex</code>.</li>
    <li>Replace <code>flex-item</code> with <code>nhsuk-flex-item</code>.</li>
    <li>Replace <code>govuk-media-query</code> with <code>nhsuk-media-query</code>.</li>
    <li>Replace <code>nhsuk-link-style-white</code> with <code>nhsuk-link-style-reverse</code>.</li>
    <li>Replace <code>nhsuk-text-color</code> with <code>nhsuk-text-colour</code>.</li>
    <li>Replace <code>nhsuk-typography-responsive</code> with <code>nhsuk-font-size</code>.</li>
    <li>Replace <code>nhsuk-typography-weight-bold</code> with <code>nhsuk-font-weight-bold</code>.</li>
    <li>Replace <code>nhsuk-typography-weight-normal</code> with <code>nhsuk-font-weight-normal</code>.</li>
    <li>Replace <code>panel</code> and <code>nhsuk-panel</code> with <code>nhsuk-card</code>.</li>
    <li>Replace <code>panel-with-label</code> and <code>nhsuk-panel-with-label</code> with <code>nhsuk-card</code>, passing <code>$variant: "feature"</code>.</li>
    <li>Replace <code>reading-width</code> with <code>nhsuk-reading-width</code>.</li>
    <li>Replace <code>remove-margin-mobile</code> with <code>nhsuk-remove-margin-mobile</code>.</li>
    <li>Replace <code>top-and-bottom</code> with <code>nhsuk-top-and-bottom</code>.</li>
    <li>Replace <code>visually-hidden</code> with <code>nhsuk-visually-hidden</code>.</li>
    <li>Replace <code>visually-hidden-focusable</code> with <code>nhsuk-visually-hidden-focusable</code>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h4 id="removed-sass-mixins">Mixins with no direct replacement</h4>

  <p>Replace <code>care-card</code>, <code>nhsuk-care-card</code>, <code>heading-label</code> and <code>nhsuk-heading-label</code> with the <a href="/design-system/components/card">card component</a>.</p>

  <p>Use <code>@media print</code> instead of <code>print-color</code>, <code>nhsuk-print-color</code>, <code>nhsuk-print-colour</code>, <code>print-hide</code> or <code>nhsuk-print-hide</code>:</p>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      .app-heading {
      -   @include nhsuk-print-colour;
      +   @media print {
      +     color: $nhsuk-print-text-colour;
      +   }
      }

      .app-actions {
      -   @include nhsuk-print-hide;
      +   @media print {
      +     display: none;
      +   }
      }
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

  <p>Instead of using <code>visually-shown</code> to undo <code>nhsuk-visually-hidden</code>, apply <code>nhsuk-visually-hidden</code> only where it is needed. This example keeps the label available to screen readers while hiding it visually below the desktop breakpoint:</p>

  {% call code() %}
    {% filter highlight("diff") %}
      .app-label {
      -   @include nhsuk-visually-hidden;
      -
      -   @include nhsuk-media-query($from: desktop) {
      -     @include visually-shown;
      +   @include nhsuk-media-query($until: desktop) {
      +     @include nhsuk-visually-hidden;
          }
      }
    {% endfilter %}
  {% endcall %}

{% endblock %}
